    "s1": { "color": "teal", "w": 340, "x": 3270, "y": 1780, "text": "Safe, caution and danger switch on the mobile check board via the demo chips. These four are the cases with no verdict.\n\nThe hatched band never renders an exact water level — the page does not know the real total, so a precise level would be either a lie or a disclosure." },
    "s2": { "color": "orange", "w": 340, "x": 1830, "y": 4880, "text": "The differentiator.\n\nThe slider defaults to a number that flips DANGER to SAFE. Generate certificate → 2.6s pause → REFUSED.\n\nThe copy has to stay honest: the failure happens on the landlord's machine, before a proof exists. Nothing was submitted and nothing was rejected." },
    "s3": { "color": "blue", "w": 340, "x": 1970, "y": 3240, "text": "Colour: obangsaek / dancheong.\n\nCheong blue-green, hwang ochre, jeok vermilion — the temple-eave palette — over hanji ivory, with the navy-and-cobalt chrome of Korean public and financial services.\n\nRed still reads as danger here because this is safety signage (KOSHA/ISO), not a price direction — on KRX red means up." }
  }
